  "body_markdown": "Skip to content\n\nDental Implants\n\nDental Implant Surgery\n\nAll-on-4 Dental Implants\n\nFixed Teeth vs. Removable\n\nCost & Compare\n\nDental Implant FAQ\n\nAesthetics\n\nCosmetic Dentistry\n\nPorcelain Veneers\n\nDental Crowns & Bridges\n\nSmile Makeover\n\nTeeth Whitening\n\nTreatments\n\nSedation Dentistry\n\nOral Surgery\n\nEmergency Dentistry\n\nConditions We Treat\n\nWhat To Expect\n\nPatient Center\n\nInsurance & Financing\n\nSmile Gallery\n\nWho We Are\n\nWhy Choose Us\n\nMeet Dr. Esam Nahlah\n\nMeet The Team\n\nVideo Library\n\nPatient Stories\n\nFor Doctors\n\nReferral Form\n\nContact Us\n\nBlog\n\nCurrent Patients\n\nTysons Corner: (703) 448-3312\n\nAlexandria: (703) 940-5410\n\nNew Patients\n\nTysons Corner: (571) 619-9442\n\nAlexandria: (571) 410-3430\n\nBook now\n\n\n## Book Now\n\n\n\n## Book Now\n\n\n\n## Unraveling the Complexities: Complications in Implant Dentistry\n\n\nJuly 20, 2024\n\n\n#### Share This Post\n\n\nDental implants in McLean, VA, replace missing teeth’ root parts. These fixtures are fastened directly into the jawbone through a surgical procedure, providing a solid base for artificial teeth known as crowns. This technique is highly valued, helping people regain their smiles, confidence, and full-mouth functionality.\n\nComplications in implant dentistry’ refer to challenges, problems, or detrimental outcomes of dental implants. These complications range from minor issues, such as mild discomfort or swelling, to more severe complications, such as infection or nerve damage. It’s essential to be aware that these potential issues exist and are inherent risks of the procedure.\n\n\n## Diving into Certain Complications in McLean, VA\n\n\nNow, let’s dive a little deeper into specific complications. Nerve damage, sinus problems, and infection are three common issues in implant dentistry. These problems can potentially hinder daily functions and impact quality of life.\n\nSeveral factors can contribute to these complications, such as inadequate post-operative care or an inexperienced implant surgeon. Using improper materials or techniques during the implant procedure can also increase the risk of these complications.\n\n\n## How to Prevent Complications in Implant Dentistry\n\n\nPrevention is always better than cure. The same rule applies to implant dentistry. Proper care, follow-up, and maintenance of the implant, combined with the skill and proficiency of a professional implant surgeon, can significantly minimize the possibility of complications.\n\nPatients can ensure the longevity and success of their dental implants by following a strict oral hygiene routine and attending regular dental check-ups. Maintaining a balanced diet can also play a significant role in promoting overall oral health and preventing potential complications in implant dentistry.\n\n\n## The Role of Tackling Implant Complications\n\n\nOur practice has deep dental expertise and uses sound procedures and protocols to troubleshoot potential implant complications. In essence, the right dental professional can reduce dental worries despite the possible complications involved in implant dentistry.\n\nAre you ready to restore your smile with dental implants at our skilled and trusted implant dentistry practice? Please don’t wait to get the smile of your dreams with us. Contact Dr. Nahlah and our exceptional team at our implant office in McLean, VA, to schedule an appointment today!\n\nPrevPreviousComplete Teeth Replacement: The Perks of Dental Implants Explained\n\nNextNavigating the Path to Smile Restoration: Unveiling the Secrets of Implants of TeethNext\n\n\n#### More To Explore\n\n\n\n### Unlock the Benefits of Dental Implants: Your Best Teeth Replacement Option\n\n\nTooth loss can become an unfortunate reality for many as we age. Thankfully, advancements in dental technology, like dental implants,\n\nRead More »\n\nOctober 26, 2024\n\n\n### Your Comprehensive Guide on Dental Implants: The Best Replacement of Tooth Solution\n\n\nDental implants in McLean, VA are small, and titanium posts are surgically placed in your jawbone underneath your gum line.\n\nOctober 20, 2024\n\n\n## You Are Welcome Here.\n\n\nSchedule your consultation today.\n\nFacebook Instagram Youtube Google\n\n\n#### Contact Us\n\n\nAddresses:\n\nTysons Corner\n\n7901 Jones Branch Dr., Suite 220\n\nMcLean, VA 22102\n\nNew Patients: (571) 619-9442\n\nCurrent Patients: (703) 448-3312\n\nAlexandria\n\n2855 Duke St,\n\nAlexandria, VA 22314\n\nNew Patients: (571) 410-3430\n\nCurrent Patients: (703) 940-5410\n\n\n#### Hours\n\n\nMonday: 8:00am – 5:00pm\n\nTuesday: 8:00am – 5:00pm\n\nWednesday: 8:00am – 5:00pm\n\nThursday: 8:00am – 5:00pm\n\nFriday: 8:00am – 2:00pm\n\nSaturday: Closed\n\nSunday: Closed\n\n\n#### Services\n\n\nAll-On-4® Implants\n\nCrowns & Bridges\n\n\n#### About Us\n\n\nMeet the Doctor\n\nAbout Us\n\nBefore & After Photos\n\n2025 Dr. Nahlah. All rights reserved",
